From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chinohana <chinohana@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: allow SukiSU install-fd supercall through seccomp

SukiSU-Ultra v4.1.3 asks the kernel for an anonymous control FD using
two magic arguments to reboot(2).  Android blocks reboot for app
processes before the sys_enter tracepoint and reboot kprobe can see it.

Bypass seccomp only for that exact SukiSU request.  All other reboot
calls and all other syscalls retain the native seccomp policy.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/ptrace.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/ptrace.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/ptrace.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/ptrace.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/ptrace.c
@@ -51,6 +51,10 @@
 #define CREATE_TRACE_POINTS
 #include <trace/events/syscalls.h>
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU
+extern bool ksu_is_install_fd_syscall(int nr, const struct pt_regs *regs);
+#endif
+
 struct pt_regs_offset {
 	const char *name;
 	int offset;
@@ -1859,7 +1863,11 @@ int syscall_trace_enter(struct pt_regs *regs)
 		tracehook_report_syscall(regs, PTRACE_SYSCALL_ENTER);
 
 	/* Do the secure computing after ptrace; failures should be fast. */
-	if (secure_computing(NULL) == -1)
+	if (
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU
+	    !ksu_is_install_fd_syscall(regs->syscallno, regs) &&
+#endif
+	    secure_computing(NULL) == -1)
 		return -1;
 
 	if (test_thread_flag(TIF_SYSCALL_TRACEPOINT))
-- 
2.53.0.windows.2
